        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(subagents): native announceTarget for subagent completion routing (#27445)",
        "body": "## 2026-07-20 refresh\n\n- Exact head dbd3545b8967de7cae93d5ab42925feb7226ffa9 merges upstream main bf6961d33efc1bc0883fd4fce898bb680ed7ba87.\n- Exact-head GitHub CI and the post-body proof workflows completed with no failures. Generated config/Kysely/prompt checks plus touched-file formatting, lint, and diff checks passed before push.\n- The concrete detached fan-in workflow requested by ClawSweeper is documented in comment 5025541882. The older live receipt below remains historical behavior evidence; the current refresh preserved the opt-in internal-only contract but did not rerun that live harness.\n\nFixes #27445\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nSubagent completions normally follow OpenClaw's existing completion-delivery policy. Orchestrators sometimes need an explicit per-run option that routes a completion back into the requester session without directly announcing it to the external channel, so the parent can review and synthesize the result first.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdds an optional native `announceTarget: \"parent\"` argument to `sessions_spawn`:\n\n- explicit `\"parent\"` wakes the requester session through the existing `subagent_announce` path with `deliver:false`\n- parent-targeted delivery is fail-closed: it does not fall back to the external channel if requester wakeup fails\n- omitting `announceTarget` preserves the existing completion behavior; there is no new channel default\n- the option is per-spawn only; there is no global or per-agent config key\n- thread-bound `thread:true, mode:\"session\"` spawns can register parent-targeted completion while retaining their active child-thread behavior\n- the nullable per-run choice is persisted in the subagent registry and SQLite so a pending completion keeps its route across restart\n- ACP `streamTo` remains separate; `announceTarget` is native-only and does not map to ACP streaming\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `9d153136fc27495e68dc9a793b4cc4aebd5612d4`\n\n- GitHub CI: 116 checks complete, 0 failures, 0 pending; `openclaw/ci-gate`, lint, production/test types, docs, security, and runtime-boundary lanes are green.\n- Focused routing/registry tests: 281 passed.\n- Gateway-supervision regression tests: 33 passed.\n- Exact-head live proof: explicit parent routing, omitted/default behavior, and SQLite restart replay all passed.\n- Redacted proof receipt: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/101248#issuecomment-4995141547\n\nThe live proof used an isolated scratch Gateway and fake conversation targets. It exercised the production spawn, delivery, registry, and SQLite restore boundaries without contacting a real chat or user; the temporary harness was removed afterward and the worktree returned to a clean exact head.",
